The quay at Saltmarsh, early morning. Nets, crates, a painted sign: WELCOME INSPECTOR. TOBIAS is up a ladder, nailing bunting to the sign. HETTIE watches from below with a basket of fish.

HETTIE
Tobias, the sign is upside down.

TOBIAS
It is not upside down. It is *festive*.

HETTIE
It says ROTCEPSNI.

TOBIAS
(climbing down to look)
Well. He’ll be coming from the sea side. From the sea it will read perfectly.

HETTIE
He’s coming on the coach.

TOBIAS
Then he can stand on his head. Hettie, this man decides whether the light stays lit. If it goes dark, the boats go home blind and the town goes with them. I want him to love us.

HETTIE
Then don’t nail anything to him.

TOBIAS
I’m only nailing things *near* him.

A coach horn, off. They freeze.

HETTIE
That’s him.

TOBIAS
Smile. Fish. Look prosperous.

HETTIE holds up a fish. TOBIAS straightens the sign, which falls down.

> LIGHTS FADE.
